    "body": "Implements the CSS selector parser and matcher specified in ADR-008 (`docs/decisions/008-css-selectors.md`).\n\n## Background\n\nADR-008 decided that we implement selector matching ourselves in a new `renderer/css/` module, rather than using lexbor's selectors module. The reasons:\n\n- lexbor's selectors operate on lexbor's tree, coupling Phase 2 to lexbor (violates ADR-007)\n- We'd have to parse selectors ourselves anyway to extract specificity\n- The tree-walk is needed in Phase 3 (layout) and Phase 4 (paint)\n- Selector matching is a core educational goal of the project\n\n## Scope\n\n### New module: `honeybee::renderer::css`\n\n- `src/renderer/css/selectors.hpp` — public API\n- `src/renderer/css/selectors.cpp` — parser + matcher\n- `tests/test_selectors.cpp` — unit tests\n\n### API\n\n```cpp\nstruct Specificity {\n    unsigned a, b, c;\n    friend bool operator<(const Specificity&, const Specificity&);\n};\n\nclass Selector {\npublic:\n    static std::optional<Selector> parse(std::string_view text);\n    bool matches(const dom::Node&) const;\n    Specificity specificity() const;\n};\n\nclass SelectorList {\npublic:\n    static std::optional<SelectorList> parse(std::string_view text);\n    std::optional<Specificity> matches(const dom::Node&) const;\n};\n```\n\n### Supported syntax (v1)\n\n- Type selectors (`div`), universal (`*`)\n- Class (`.foo`), ID (`#main`)\n- Attribute: presence, `=`, `^=`, `$=`, `*=`, `~=`, `|=`\n- Combinators: descendant, child (`>`), adjacent sibling (`+`), general sibling (`~`)\n- Selector lists (`A, B, C`)\n- Compound selectors (`div.foo#bar[data-x=\"1\"]`)\n\n### Specificity\n\nPer CSS 2.1: `(a, b, c)` = (ids, classes+attributes, types). Compared lexicographically. Universal `*` contributes 0.\n\n### Deferred (explicitly out of scope)\n\n- Pseudo-classes (`:hover`, `:nth-child()`, `:not()`, ...)\n- Pseudo-elements (`::before`, `::after`)\n- Namespaces (`svg|rect`)\n- Level 4 extensions (`:has()`, `:is()`, `:where()`)\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `renderer/css/selectors.hpp` and `selectors.cpp` compile into `honeybee_lib`\n- [ ] Tests in `tests/test_selectors.cpp` cover every supported syntax form\n- [ ] Malformed selectors return `std::nullopt` (e.g. `parse(\"div >\")`)\n- [ ] Specificity arithmetic correct for all compound-selector combinations\n- [ ] Combinator traversal tested on a multi-level DOM tree\n- [ ] `grep -rl \"lexbor/\" src/` still returns exactly `src/renderer/html/convert.cpp`\n- [ ] CI green\n\n## Notes\n\n- Sibling combinators require locating a node's index inside `parent()->children()`. For our scale, a linear scan is fine; see ADR-008's 'Sibling lookup' consequence.\n- `renderer::dom::Node` will need no changes for v1.\n\n## Refs\n\n- ADR-008: `docs/decisions/008-css-selectors.md`\n- ADR-007: `docs/decisions/007-dom-ownership.md`\n- ADR-001, ADR-006",
